insert into rubric_criteria (role_code, sort, name, description, weight) values ('SPM', 1, $q$Unasked Fix$q$, $q$Meets everything the PM version of this criterion asks for (The CV names a specific problem that was nobody's assigned job, such as a process, tool, checklist or workflow gap, and says the candidate built the fix themselves. It says why they noticed it, for example because they were doing or watching the work. Score high if all three are present: a named problem, "no one asked," and something concrete that was built. Score low if the CV only lists features shipped from a roadmap.) and, in addition, the fix reached beyond the candidate's own team, into other teams, functions or clients. Nobody sponsored or approved it beforehand. It changed a standard, process or system that others now depend on. Score high only if the CV shows a cross-team reach and a change that outlasted the original problem. A fix used only by the candidate's own immediate team caps at a mid score.$q$, 25)
